    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42207" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Saddūcaei</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Sadducees</i>, <i>a religious sect
				among the Jews</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert. Praescr.
			45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt. 3, 7</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Saddūcaeus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the Sadducees</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 3, p. 134</span></i>
			.</div>
